codex
The failure is reproducibly caused by the audit sandbox’s PID view: processes see a namespace PID whose `/proc/<pid>/exe` entry is absent, and Lean 4.22 aborts while resolving its own executable. I’m applying a narrow audit-only compatibility shim that supplies the truthful installed path for only `/proc/*/exe` lookups, then rerunning the unchanged trusted preflight. The shim source, build command, and tests will remain in evidence.
apply patch
